{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For</b> — because it is at the etnaḥta of <b>Shechem</b>, [there] <b>Shechem</b> is one. The meaning is that they are joined, in the manner of: \"and I shall distress them from every side, that they may be found\" [translator's literal rendering]." "<b>And the word תכונן</b> — an abbreviated form, for the meaning is: You set the bow with arrows."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The verse cited (והצרותי להם למען ימצאו) does not correspond to any standard biblical verse exactly; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:08.321675784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}